  "  ""I-177"": ""the author's message of 2026-10-12 (the automaton: I-167, I-170, I-171 as its transition function, indices 59, 63, 127 as its input); section 3 corrected the same day (60 ⊕ 68 = 120; the pole is 60 ⊕ 128 = 188)"","
  "  ""I-178"": ""the author, 2026-10-12, through the other assistant's write-ups: \""the connecting rule is the allocated raw buffer, because entropy degradation is a signal\""; \""it should be xored by user agent\""; \""all the data is static indices, we are considering the routing; the values come from the proxy and the reflect of the user literals from their proof tree\""; the static indices are \""positions to hold to keep the same frame in view or same window\""; \""Windows and document so fs gs rs us can explain it\""; \""the Catch-22 is: all change is outside the system\"". The positional reading (a separator is a separator by its place, so routed 0x1C-0x1F pass as data unescaped) is derived from \""static indices\"", not stated by the author in those words"","
  "  ""I-179"": ""the author, 2026-10-12: \""the 4gb is virtual\""; measured on the TOSHIBA (Node 24): a 2^32-byte buffer and a full wasm32 memory allocate, with resident memory growing only by the touched pages"","
  "  ""I-180"": ""the author, 2026-10-12: \""64MB has 4GB worth of virtual memory\"", \""16 bits has 8MB\""; asked, \""x86 initializes a virtual 4gb\"", and yes, the 8 MB is the tables that map it; measured on the TOSHIBA (i5-6300U, x86_64, 4 KB pages, Node 24): touching one byte in each 2 MB of a 2^32-byte buffer grows VmPTE by 8212 kB and resident memory by 8 MB, and the check holds under systemd-run MemoryMax=64M, where touching 128 MB is killed"","
  "  ""I-182"": ""the author's notes in _archive/_deprecated/4320 (BQF.md: \""7! = 5040 ;; incidences of factors\"", the rows 5040/7 to 5040/37, \""Tell me when it breaks\""; _4320.finding.md: the slot f*720 + t*180 + p; Pure.Typescript.Functions.md: Q, the LFSR A and the step Δ), run as DeepSeek's ten-claim write-up in _archive/_chat_history/Describing the Atlas.md; the author, 2026-10-13: \""it's not the wrong value but the wrong position, or for us, index\"""","
