  "  ""I-187"": ""the author, 2026-10-13: \""tripods of trigintaduonions of the 64-nions\"", with Wikipedia's Trigintaduonion page pasted (its 155 triples, citing OEIS A171477)"","
  "  ""I-188"": ""the author, 2026-10-13: \""frame 4 sub frame 4 index 19 from the http is the 19 of the 64 from 0-63 bytes of the atomics compare and exchange 19,128,63\"", with RFC 2616 section 19.4.4 (Introduction of Content-Encoding, as pasted); \""base 36 44J\""; \""the 5, 3, 4, 7 coordinate\"""","
  "  ""I-189"": ""the author, 2026-10-13, pasted Wikipedia's \""Sum of two cubes\"" (ending: \""19 is the total of the digits in 1729; 19 reversed is 91; 19 x 91 is 1729\"") and \""Difference of two squares\"", without words of their own; the triplet (7, 13, 19) is I-183; then: \""that's the measurement of the two prime gap\"""","
  "  ""I-191"": ""the author, 2026-10-13: \""it's for rebuilding, based on the Fano lottery and trigintaduonion triples, so always 14 logic steps away\"", then MathWorld's Fano plane entry (the Transylvania lottery: two Fano planes, 14 tickets for three numbers from 1-14)"","
